# Publicly known secret values, as SHA-256 hashes (one per line: "<hash>  <where it came from>").
#
# Every value that a secret variable ever had in a tracked file of Oliva, plus the
# placeholders and the CI values. All of them are in a public git history, so a service
# running on one of them has no secret at all. The env check and the backend entrypoint
# refuse them in production (docs/roadmap/epics/E-config-contract.md).
#
# Append-only: a value is added the day it leaks and is never removed. An app does NOT
# edit this file (it is Oliva's); a value that leaked in an app is rotated there.
# To add one:   printf %s 'the-value' | sha256sum
# It lives under backend/ because the backend image needs the same list (build context).
d528f71466ab8431ab8566ab8df14eeb7db08dee3729d1bdb3f3e48b853df657  APP_SECRET committed in .env.backend until 1.6.0
2addc9b29c8e04e7f2791ec68223b16adc9cf106017c53893ae9fa3c2246634f  JWT_PASSPHRASE committed in .env.backend until 1.6.0
